Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Exact solution of the likelihood", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d95bb4ab-bd4e-4daf-9ab6-2c45247c0f97"],

Cell["\<\
By Eq. (14) every residual is R = u + \[Nu] w + Log A, with u and w fixed by \
the data, so \[Chi]^2 is an exact quadratic form in the two parameters (Log \
A, \[Nu]). The minimum therefore follows from a single linear solve, the \
covariance is twice the inverse Hessian, and the \[CapitalDelta]\[Chi]^2 = 1, \
4, 9 intervals on A are exactly A exp(\[PlusMinus]n\[Sigma]) with \[Sigma] \
the marginal width in Log A. This replaces the FindMinimum/FindRoot calls of \
the original notebook, which is where its FindMinimum::lstol warnings came \
from.

sigmaLogAEq16 is the independent closed form of Eq. (16), valid at fixed \
\[Nu]; the check cell below confirms that the quadratic form reproduces the \
direct definition of Section 2 and that the two expressions for the \
conditional width agree.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab7ae6f8-86f1-4762-a281-755a7991aab4"],

